:"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/deployments"},"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/commits/a49c67683575eaef041cfb9c065e84b67ca49ce9","sha":"a49c67683575eaef041cfb9c065e84b67ca49ce9","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MTMxODYwNDcwMjphNDljNjc2ODM1NzVlYWVmMDQxY2ZiOWMwNjVlODRiNjdjYTQ5Y2U5","html_url":"https://github.com/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/commit/a49c67683575eaef041cfb9c065e84b67ca49ce9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/commits/a49c67683575eaef041cfb9c065e84b67ca49ce9/comments","commit":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/git/commits/a49c67683575eaef041cfb9c065e84b67ca49ce9","author":{"date":"2026-09-15T20:18:56.000+05:30","name":"Ambuj Upadhyay","email":"34904987+lets-order-some-fries@users.noreply.github.com"},"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T20:18:56.000+05:30","name":"Ambuj Upadhyay","email":"34904987+lets-order-some-fries@users.noreply.github.com"},"message":"fix(schema): a file that cannot declare a tool is not evidence of an under-read\n\nMeasuring the partiality rule across all 400 indexed servers turned up one\nfalse positive, and it was the worst shape this change could have.\n\ndaedalusdevelopmentgroup/ddg-agent-payable-services was called under-read\nbecause a single file in its package directory went unfetched: a 25-line\n__init__.py holding a docstring, a __version__ and a lazy-import __getattr__.\nZero tool declarations. All 43 of its tools come from the two files that WERE\nread, so the surface was complete. And the punishment was a reward — cost\ncarries weight 0.15, its score of 40 sat far below the weighted mean of the\nrest, so withholding it moved the card from B 79 to A- 86. The rule handed a\nseven-point grade increase to a repository it had wrongly accused.\n\nFiles that cannot declare a tool surface are now excluded from the candidate\nuniverse of this check: package barrels (__init__.py, index.ts/js/mjs, mod.rs),\nconftest.py, and the singular test/ and spec/ directories that the existing\nisNonServerPath misses. isNonServerPath itself is deliberately left alone —\nwidening it would change what extraction reads, moving grades in ways this\nchange has not measured.\n\nThe exclusion costs something in the other direction and the comment says so:\nan unread src/tools/index.ts that genuinely holds registrations no longer\ncounts as evidence. That is acceptable because entrypoints get fetch priority\nand are almost always read, and because the alternative is calling complete\nreads partial.\n\nRe-derived over all 400 cached decision inputs with no network: flips go 6 to\n5, the only ref that stops flipping is the false positive, and all five true\npositives survive — including alexar76/aimarket-plugins, whose flip directory\nalso holds an unread __init__.py but still fires on the genuinely unread\ngateway_core.py. Verified live on the built CLI: ddg is back to B 79.\n\nTwo regression tests pin both directions: the ddg shape must not flip, and the\nindex.ts trade-off is written down rather than left implicit. The second is\ndeliberately not under a tools/ directory, because there the older fan-out\nguard fires on its own and would mask what the test is about.\n\n829 tests pass; tsc build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/git/trees/cdc7c4f36f67d5b15dbf150d06f0c59888592a23","sha":"cdc7c4f36f67d5b15dbf150d06f0c59888592a23"},"comment_count":0},"author":{"login":"lets-order-some-fries","id":34904987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTA0OTg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34904987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lets-order-some-fries","html_url":"https://github.com/lets-order-some-fries","followers_url"